!!! The class this floor's shape named, now written into the rite

''Four of six inbound edges read as LICENCES, not welds — and the rite now says so.'' `otakiage#/examples` carries this floor as its own worked row: `standing` × `floor`, ''QUOTED OUT'' — a floor whose moʻolelo has been quoted out does not retire by welding edges, because the quotes ARE the fold, already done. A hand reading //six inbound edges// as //six welds owed// would perform four welds that each destroy the record the licence cites, ''silently and permanently'' — the citation reads on unchanged while its target names a hole.

''The general form, which the rite now also carries:'' a stage that ends in deletion cannot be evidenced by a pointer. Both halves of that law came out of this floor's own measurement.

!!! ★ The code dependency that only code can cut ★

Six code sites cite this carrier: `packages/lararium-mesh/src/realm-bag.ts:4` and `:459` · `tests/cas-transit.test.ts:97` · `tests/stowage-clock.test.ts:9` · `tests/ahi-ka.test.ts:119` and `:134`. Five of those read as comments. ''One is a live assertion.''

`packages/lararium-mesh/tests/ahi-ka.test.ts:141` READS this file off disk, regex-extracts the three ahi-kā parameters this floor quotes, and holds them against `AHI_KA_500YR` in the module, failing with //"the canon teaches ratios the code no longer runs — re-stamp scale-stories-basket-one.mem"//. ⚠ ''DELETING THIS CARRIER REDS THAT TEST.'' Any fire folds the ratio prose to wherever the assertion should point next, or moves the assertion, ''before'' the burn — and the test's own sibling CONTROL (//the constant carries all three fields, so the comparison above is not vacuous//) must stay honest through the move.

!!! The shape worth naming, beyond the mechanics

''Four of the six inbound carriers QUOTE this floor as the RECORD of an operator ruling'', under quote license, rather than leaning on it for argument. That reads as a question for the rite rather than a defect here: ''a talk-story floor whose moʻolelo has been quoted out does not retire by welding edges — the quotes ARE the fold, already done, and what remains is the empty vessel plus the licences pointing at it.'' Does such a floor retire by DELETION, or does it become the citable source those licences name? `otakiage` rules neither today. Until it does, a hand reading //six inbound edges// as //six welds owed// will do four welds that destroy the thing the licence cites.

